  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $r\\in {r,t}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $s$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $t\\in {r,t}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $u$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $v$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $w$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $x\\in {x,y,z}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $y\\in {x,y,z}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $z\\in {x,y,z}\\,\u2713$\n\nThe elements $s,u,v,$ and $w$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${s,u,v,w}.$",
